[center][size=6][b]OVERLAY MAP[/b][/size]
[size=4]A hologram world map that opens over the game with one key.
Built to be lightweight, so you can use it without pausing your gameplay.[/size][/center]

[line]

[size=5][b]What it is[/b][/size]
The vanilla map pauses the game and takes over the screen. Overlay Map is a 2D map of the whole city that opens as a hologram panel right where you are, while the world keeps moving behind it. Check where you are, find the next gig, set a waypoint and close it again, without ever leaving the street.

It draws the vanilla map's own roads and buildings, shows the game's markers with their vanilla icons, and mirrors your GPS routes.

[line]

[size=5][b]Features[/b][/size]
[list]
[*][b]The whole city.[/b] Roads and buildings come from the game's own map data, Dogtown and the Badlands included. Zoom from single buildings out to all of Night City.
[*][b]Vanilla markers.[/b] Quests, gigs, NCPD, vendors, fast travel and more, with the game's own icons. Put a marker near the centre to see its details in the sidebar. Map filters turn each category on or off.
[*][b]Waypoints.[/b] E works like right-clicking on the vanilla map: set a custom waypoint on an empty spot, make a job active, track a marker, or clear what you're tracking.
[*][b]GPS routes.[/b] Your waypoint route and the tracked quest's route are drawn as flowing dots.
[*][b]Area names.[/b] The sidebar names the area and district under the cursor, in your game language.
[*][b]Collectibles.[/b] Shards, tarot graffiti, iconic weapons, legendary cyberware and clothing, and skill shards each get a pin. Collected ones stay on the map, scratched out.
[*][b]Fast travel and teleport.[/b] Fast travel from any fast travel marker, or teleport V (and V's car) anywhere on the map. The teleport key can be switched off.
[*][b]NCART lines.[/b] An optional filter draws the five metro lines in their colours.
[*][b]Photo pins.[/b] Photos you take in photo mode are pinned where you took them and kept between sessions, with a thumbnail in the sidebar.
[*][b]Five colour themes.[/b] Cyan, Red, Green, Purple and Amber, or follow your HUD Painter colours.
[*][b]Make it yours.[/b] Panel size and opacity, map brightness and contrast, road glow, scanlines, and an optional VHS tracking band and glitch.
[*][b]Hold to show.[/b] Optionally keep the map up only while the key is held.
[/list]

[line]

[size=5][b]Controls[/b][/size]
[b]O[/b] opens and closes the map (it does nothing in menus or photo mode). You can rebind it, or use a combo such as [b]Ctrl + M[/b], in Mod Settings.

[b]Keyboard and mouse (default).[/b] While the map is open it takes the keyboard and mouse, and V stands still:
[list]
[*]Pan: [b]move the mouse[/b], or W A S D / the arrow keys
[*]Zoom: mouse wheel
[*]Follow V again: Space
[*]Act on the selected marker: F
[*]Set waypoint / track: E or Enter
[*]Teleport / fast travel: Q
[*]Cycle marker filter: R
[/list]
Prefer to keep turning the camera with the mouse? Switch off [i]Mouse pans the map[/i] in Mod Settings.

[b]Numpad.[/b] Choose [i]V keeps moving (numpad)[/i] in Mod Settings and the map uses only the numpad, so you can keep walking and driving while it's open.

[b]Controller.[/b] Hold View for half a second to open the map (a tap still opens the pause menu). Left stick pans, LT/RT zoom, A acts, RB sets a waypoint, X teleports, Y cycles the filter, R3 follows V, B closes.

Every key can be rebound in Mod Settings → Overlay Map.

[line]

[size=5][b]Requirements[/b][/size]
[list]
[*]Cyberpunk 2077 [b]2.5[/b]
[*][url=https://www.nexusmods.com/cyberpunk2077/mods/1511]redscript[/url]
[*][url=https://www.nexusmods.com/cyberpunk2077/mods/7780]Codeware[/url]
[*][url=https://www.nexusmods.com/cyberpunk2077/mods/2380]RED4ext[/url]
[/list]
[b]Optional:[/b] [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/cyberpunk2077/mods/4885]Mod Settings[/url], for the settings menu and key rebinding. Without it every option keeps its default.

[line]

[size=5][b]Installation[/b][/size]
Install with Vortex or Mod Organizer 2, or unzip into your Cyberpunk 2077 folder (the one with [i]bin[/i], [i]archive[/i] and [i]r6[/i]).

[b]Uninstall:[/b] delete these three:
[list]
[*]archive/pc/mod/OverlayMap.archive
[*]r6/scripts/OverlayMap/
[*]red4ext/plugins/OverlayMapNative/
[/list]

[line]

[size=5][b]Known issues[/b][/size]
[list]
[*]Waypoints use a small RED4ext plugin, tested on game 2.5. If it can't find the game function it needs, waypoints switch off and everything else keeps working.
[*]The game's HUD fades out while the map is open. Display → [i]Hide HUD while open[/i] turns that off.
[*]On a game version other than 2.5 the map shows a notice that some places may not match.
[/list]

[line]

[size=5][b]For mod authors[/b][/size]
Other mods can add their own items to the map through a layer API. Ask in the comments if you'd like to use it.
